# Cloudflare Pages response headers (efficiency audit 2026-10 #15).
#
# Everything under /assets/ is content-hashed by Vite: a changed file gets a
# new name, so a cached copy can never be stale. Without this rule Pages serves
# them `public, max-age=0, must-revalidate`, and every visit without the
# service worker (a first visit, a hard reload, a managed Chromebook that
# clears site data) revalidates each chunk with its own round trip.
#
# NOTHING ELSE is listed on purpose: index.html and the service worker must
# keep revalidating, or a deploy could not reach a returning visitor.
/assets/*
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=31536000, immutable
